step_details.raw_response:
Thought: Test a simple robust mean on the full pool to establish a baseline.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool_full"}

Thought: Test a weighted combination using inverse error weights on the full model pool to see if it improves over the mean baseline.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a robust median combination on the full model pool to see if it outperforms the weighted mean.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool_full"}

Thought: Test a trimmed_mean combination on the full pool to see if trimming outliers improves over the median baseline.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","pool":"pool_full","trim_pct":0.2}

Thought: Test a weighted combination using the pooled_meta_model handle (w1) on the full model pool to see if it outperforms trimmed_mean.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"w1"}

Thought: Test a simple mean on the smaller, high‑rank pool1 to see if restricting to top models improves performance.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool1"}

Thought: Test a weighted inverse-error combination on the smaller, high‑rank pool1 to see if the weighting improves over the simple mean on that pool.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool1","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a DBA combination on the smaller, high‑rank pool1 to see if iterative Bayesian averaging improves over the mean/trimmed‑mean baselines.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"dba","pool":"pool1","dba_max_iter":30}

Thought: Test a simple mean on pool2 to see if a larger pool with some extra models improves over the best DBA result.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool2"}

Thought: Test a DBA on the full model pool to see if expanding the pool improves over the best DBA on pool1.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"dba","pool":"pool_full","dba_max_iter":30}

Thought: Test a robust median on the high‑rank pool1 to see if it beats the DBA baseline.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","models":["rf","DWT_rf","FT_rf","FT_catboost","NaiveMovingAverage"]}

Thought: Test a weighted combination on the full pool using inverse_error weights to see if expanding to all models improves over the best robust median.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a weighted combination on pool2 using inverse_error weights to see if a smaller but still diverse pool improves over mean and DBA on pool2.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool2","weights":"inverse_error"}

